
@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Inputs}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_TimeInput}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Usage}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Time_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Time_Input @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage</h1>

<p>
    The example below shows the Time Input component being bound to both non-nullable and nullable <span class="code-span">TimeOnly</span> fields. The "End Time" and "Start Time" are non-nullable, required, with  
    validation rules that says the "End Time" must be greater than the start time and with a "Start Time" that must be between 7am and 10am.
</p>
<p>
    Rather than set the component parameter <span class="code-span">Required</span> to true, which only adds a red asterisk to the label and the <span class="code-span">aria-required</span> attribute to the inputs, I have opted to
    just use the text "Required" in the hint text for the required field, and the text "Optional" in the optional nullable fields. By default the required parameter is set to true so I set this to false for the Work start and end fields. 
</p>
<p>
    For both the "Start Time" and "Start Work" fields I have set the <span class="code-span">UpdateOnInput</span> parameter to true, and false for the end time and work fields just so you can see the different approaches.
    For validation on the work field, I validation rules that says if entered "Start Work" must be before 11am and if entered "End Work" must be after 1pm. As these are nullable fields and validation will run on every keystroke for "Start Work", the <span>ParseErrorMessage</span> parameter will be utilised until a valid time can
    be parsed from the inputs.
</p>

<p>
    I have used <span class="code-span">ValidationDisplayMode="TabbableWithHint"</span> on all fields. For the nullable fields I have set the <span>EnableSeconds</span> parameter to false to hide the seconds input.
</p>
<p>
    <b>Note: </b>I have used my open source Validation framework and its Blazor NuGet package <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Validated_Blazor_Repo_Site" target="_blank">Validated.Blazor (opens in new window)</a>.
    but you can use any validators that work with Blazors <span class="code-span">EditContext</span>. 
</p>

<section class="section-box">
    <h2>Time input example</h2>

    <EditForm EditContext="@_editContext" OnValidSubmit="HandleSubmit">
        
        <BlazorValidated TEntity="ScheduleDto" BoxedValidators="_boxedValidators" AddDisplayName="true" />

        <div class="br-input-row">
            <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="Start Time" @bind-Value="@_scheduleData.StartTime" HintText="Required, the time (24-hour format) you want the scheduled action to start." 
                Required="false" EnableSeconds="true" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="true" ParseErrorMessage="Must be a valid time."  
                ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.TabbableWithHint" />

            <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="End Time" @bind-Value="@_scheduleData.EndTime" HintText="Required, the time (24-hour format) you want the scheduled action to finish"
                Required="false" EnableSeconds="true" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="false" ParseErrorMessage="Must be a valid time."   
                ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.TabbableWithHint" />
        </div>
         <div class="br-input-row">

            <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="Start Work" @bind-Value="@_scheduleData.StartWork" HintText="Optional, the time (24-hour format) you start work." Required="false"
                       EnableSeconds="false" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="true"  ParseErrorMessage="Must be a valid time."  
                       ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.TabbableWithHint" />

            <TimeInput class="br-col-xs-12 br-col-sm-6" LabelText="End Work" @bind-Value="@_scheduleData.EndWork" HintText="Optional, the time (24-hour format) you finish work." Required="false"
                       EnableSeconds="false" DataPosition="DataPosition.Start" UpdateOnInput="false" ParseErrorMessage="Must be a valid time."  
                       ValidationDisplayMode="ValidationDisplayMode.TabbableWithHint" />
        </div>
        <div class="br-input-row">
            <button class="br-col-xs-12 normal-button" type="submit">Fake Submit to trigger validation on unmodified fields</button>
        </div>
    </EditForm>


</section>
<p style="padding-block:1rem;">
    Below is the code that was used for the example. Please note that in general when using the Validated library the validators would be in a shared library so they could be used in any part of your application.
</p>
<CodeBox CodeBlock="@InputSnippets.Time_Input_Code_Example" AriaLabel="Time input code example" />
